      "writtenOn": "2026-11-12T17:21:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks Manoj. Sure, I can add default: 0 in the ComponentIntegrity PDI saying \"A value of zero indicates that no component-integrity information has been acquired yet.\"\n\nToday, https://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/bmcweb/+/88828/15/redfish-core/lib/component_integrity.hpp#159 skips LastUpdated when it is zero, so no epoch timestamp is shown. And looks like the https://redfish.dmtf.org/schemas/v1/ComponentIntegrity.v1_4_0.json schema also allows null, so returning null when the timestamp is unavailable looks like an option.\n\nQuick doubt on LastUpdated - PDI mentions firmware and certificate changes. Today, spdmd gets that information during the signed-measurement request. Should the timestamp update after every successful measurement request, even if the values are unchanged, or only when a change in the integrity information is detected? (For the second one, I think spdmd does not monitor those change events separately or compare measurements across requests.)",
      "parentUuid": "b03e40b3_1a365c94",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 78,
        "startChar": 7,
        "endLine": 80,
        "endChar": 35
